  "title": "NEWLEADER quorum commits a DIFF history that acknowledging learners have only enqueued",
  "cause": "At NEWLEADER the learner persists currentEpoch and only enqueues the DIFF proposals to the asynchronous SyncRequestProcessor before writing the NEWLEADER ACK that commits the leader's initial history.",
  "trigger": "Leader re-elected with an uncommitted logged txn DIFF-syncs both learners; they ACK NEWLEADER and crash before their SyncThread forces the txn; the learners then elect a new leader.",
  "consequence": "A transaction the old leader served after the NEWLEADER quorum is missing on the new leader (committed data lost).",
  "sites": [
    "zookeeper-server/src/main/java/org/apache/zookeeper/server/quorum/Learner.java:743-760",
    "zookeeper-server/src/main/java/org/apache/zookeeper/server/quorum/FollowerZooKeeperServer.java:82-91"
  ],
  "actions": [
    "LearnerNewLeader",
    "LearnerAckNewLeader",
    "LeaderBroadcast",
    "FsyncOne"
  ],
  "invariants": [
    "CommittedQuorumDurable",
    "CommittedAgreement"
  ],
  "premises": [
    "FollowerZooKeeperServer.logRequest only enqueues to the SyncRequestProcessor; nothing between logRequest and the NEWLEADER ACK write waits for its flush.",
    "The leader treats the NEWLEADER quorum as the commit of its loaded history and serves it.",
    "FLE ranks peer currentEpoch before zxid, so a learner that persisted the new epoch can win the next election with a shorter log."
  ],
